  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the highest-value first experiment is a simple, well-defined baseline to establish a performance reference. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the most minimal RNA configuration: a standard linear dimensionality reduction (PCA to 2000 dims), a single profile, and no aggregation or fusion complexity. This gives a clean floor for RNA-only performance and a direct comparison point for every other RNA-based variant (different encoders, multiprofile, aggregation). It is also the fastest configuration to train, preserving compute budget for the 9 remaining experiments. Establishing this baseline first lets subsequent experiments isolate whether image features, learned encoders (scvi, scgpt), multiprofile aggregation, or multimodal fusion actually add value over the simplest RNA signal."
}

